WEBVTT

00:21:57.354 --> 00:22:01.232
Many times women are on the front lines
of the climate crisis.

00:22:01.274 --> 00:22:04.110
And this is because for many communities,

00:22:04.152 --> 00:22:07.614
women have the responsibilities
of providing food,

00:22:07.614 --> 00:22:09.324
providing water for their families.

00:22:09.324 --> 00:22:10.533
MR: Many are farmers.

00:22:10.533 --> 00:22:14.079
VN: Exactly. So when,
you know, crops are drying

00:22:14.120 --> 00:22:16.706
because of, you know, too much heat,

00:22:16.706 --> 00:22:19.334
it's the women that are on those farms.

00:22:19.667 --> 00:22:23.088
When the farms are destroyed
or washed away,

00:22:23.129 --> 00:22:25.632
it's the women that are impacted,

00:22:25.673 --> 00:22:28.301
they are the ones working on those farms.

00:22:28.301 --> 00:22:29.844
When water systems dry out,

00:22:29.844 --> 00:22:32.972
it's women that have to walk
very long distances.